{
  "abstract": "In the visible game of cops and robber on a finite connected undirected graph, let c(G) be the least number of cops who can force capture. A multiscale pursuit argument gives c(G) ≤ n^(2/3 + e(n)) on every graph of order n, with one positive function e(n) tending to zero uniformly over the choice of graph. In particular, there are constants δ > 0 and C > 0 such that c(G) ≤ C n^(1 − δ) for every such graph, as asserted by the weak Meyniel conjecture. The repository also contains a separate formalization of the shorter proof giving c(G) ≤ 31 n^(3/4) log(2n).",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Jesse Geneson"
    }
  ],
